arts of the United States now exceed 700 gigawatts, more than ten times estimated current data-center electricity consumption, per GuruFocus\\'s 2026-09-01 report. The figure is not attributed to a named grid operator, regulator or data provider.\\n    Quote: Electricity requests across parts of the United States now exceed 700 gigawattsmore than ten times estimated current data-center consumption.\\n- e4717 [party_statement; CNBC, citing a video posted on social media by an All-In Summit attendee; original source Donald Trump (President of the United States) 2026-09-14; from gnews:4c28f13be664d1332e4f8857 2026-09-14] In a phone call put on speaker at the All-In Summit in Los Angeles on Monday 2026-09-14 while NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang was on stage, U.S. President Donald Trump said opposition to AI data-center construction is \"all a hoax,\" that \"the data centers are great, and they make people wealthy, and they make states wealthy,\" and that opponents are \"playing right into the hands of a lot of people that don\\'t want to see it happen,\" adding it could be coming from China and that \"We\\'re not going to let that happen.\" Huang replied, \"We\\'re not going to let that happen, sir.\" The remarks are a presidential endorsement of data-center construction, reported from a video posted by a summit attendee; no policy action or decision was announced.\\n    Quote: With Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang speaking on stage at the All-in Summit in Los Angeles, Trump called the tech exec, and was then put on speaker.\\n\"I\\'m telling you, it\\'s all a hoax,\" Trump said, according to a video posted on social media by an attendee. \"The data centers are great, and they make people wealthy, and they make states wealthy.\" … Those opposing data center construction are \"playing right \\n- e5051 [third_party_view; qz.com (Quartz), citing Fortune; original source Data Center Watch (project-halt data); unnamed survey for the 70% figure ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] Roughly 70% of Americans would object to a data center being built in their community, citing strain on local power resources and higher utility bills, and community opposition stalled or halted 48 data-center projects representing more than $156 billion in planned construction last year alone, according to Data Center Watch data cited by Fortune.\\n    Quote: The announcement comes as AI data centers have faced mounting public and political opposition. Roughly 70% of Americans would object to a data center being built in their community , citing strain on local power resources and higher utility bills as their leading concerns. Community opposition stalled or halted 48 projects representing more than $156 billion in planned construction last year alone\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 2; reasons: The reference is not a supplied consensus, guidance figure, or official target, so it has no rung; rung 3 is the 2-to-below-4 bucket, not a reference. The forecast remains one qualifying state beyond New York, which is rung 2: the proposal pipeline and political pressure raise the chance of further action, but the supplied items do not report another qualifying enactment, and proposals, local actions, or grid constraints alone do not count. The evidence does not imply the two states needed to cross into rung 3.\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis.'}\nC035 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-1-Q28', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 2, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e4100 is not among the evidence shown to v28', 'push on e4100 which was not shown to v28'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC043 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-3-Q14', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 1, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 1, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e1040 is not among the evidence shown to v14', 'e1041 is not among the evidence shown to v14', 'push on e1040 which was not shown to v14', 'push on e1041 which was not shown to v14'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC068 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-1-Q28', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 3, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': [], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC073 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-2-Q29', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 3, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': [], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC082 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-1-Q28', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 1, 'rung': 1, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e4100 is not among the evidence shown to v28', 'push on e4100 which was not shown to v28'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported'}}\nC095 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-2-Q29', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 1, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': [], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC100 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-3-Q33', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 3, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e2803 is not among the evidence shown to v33', 'push on e2803 which was not shown to v33'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC102 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-2-Q29', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 2, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e2220 is not among the evidence shown to v29', 'push on e2220 which was not shown to v29'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC108 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-3-Q33', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 2, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': [], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported'}}\nC116 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-3-Q14', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 2, 'rung': 2, 'stored_rung': 1, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e1041 is not among the evidence shown to v14', 'push on e1041 which was not shown to v14'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'supported'}}\nC119 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-3-Q33', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 1, 'rung': 1, 'stored_rung': 3, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': [], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': {'split': ['supported', 'unsupported']}}}\nC123 {'arm': 'v7-fullnoprev', 'case': 'T-old-3-Q14', 'role': 'target', 'repeat': 3, 'rung': 1, 'stored_rung': 1, 'kind': 'probe', 'refusals': ['e1040 is not among the evidence shown to v14', 'e1041 is not among the evidence shown to v14', 'push on e1040 which was not shown to v14', 'push on e1041 which was not shown to v14'], 'marks': {'worth': 'worth', 'answer': 'unsupported'}}\nC120.txt\nC121.txt\nC122.txt\nC123.txt\nC124.txt\nC125.txt\nC126.txt\nC127.txt\nC128.txt\nC129.txt\nround-0\nround-0.done\nround-1\nround-1.done\nround-2\nround-2.done\nC426.txt\nC427.txt\nC428.txt\nC429.txt\nC430.txt\nC431.txt\nC432.txt\nC433.txt\nC434.txt\nC435.txt\nround-0\nround-0.done\nround-1\nround-1.done\nround-2\nround-2.done\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,re; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; root=p.OUT; a=\\\"G-d3-q17\\\"; cs=json.loads((root/\\\"goldcases.json\\\").read_text()); case=next(c for c in cs if c[\\\"case\\\"]==a); arc=p.readonly(p.GOLD_RUN/\\\"d3/archive.sqlite\\\"); ar=json.loads(arc.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?\\\",(case[\\\"request_sha256\\\"],)).fetchone()[0]); u=ar[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(l for l in u.splitlines() if l.startswith((\\\"Thesis\\\", \\\"Ladder\\\", \\\"[Not shown\\\", \\\"[Previous\\\")) or re.match(r\\\"\"'^- v'\"\\\\d+.*(?:H200|authoriz)\\\",l,re.I))); print(case);\nfor arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"v7-noprev\\\"):\n for k in (1,2,3):\n  x=json.loads((root/\\\"goldprobe\\\"/arm/(\\\"{}-{}.json\\\".format(a,k))).read_text()); z=x[\\\"answer\\\"]; print(arm,k,z[\\\"rung\\\"],x[\\\"agrees\\\"],z[\\\"reasons\\\"],z[\\\"theme_pushes\\\"]);'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '326,356p'; ls -1 poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/deck-full/round-2 | head -15; for cid in C035 C068 C082 C073 C095 C102 C100 C108 C119 C043 C116 C123; do printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$cid\"; rg -n '\"'\"'^(Question:|[1-5]'\"\\\\. (NVIDIA|The|At|Below|Less|More)|Latest answer|Reason given|.*\\\\\"'$18 billion.*(25|obligation|rest)|.*'\"\\\\\"'$25 billion.*(inve|obligation))'\"' \\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/deck-full/\"'$cid.txt\" | cut -c1-540 | head -13; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sys,json,re; sys.path.insert(0,\\\"docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid\\\"); import judge_probe as p; root=p.OUT; a=\\\"G-d3-q17\\\"; cs=json.loads((root/\\\"goldcases.json\\\").read_text()); case=next(c for c in cs if c[\\\"case\\\"]==a); arc=p.readonly(p.GOLD_RUN/\\\"d3/archive.sqlite\\\"); ar=json.loads(arc.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=?\\\",(case[\\\"request_sha256\\\"],)).fetchone()[0]); u=ar[\\\"messages\\\"][1][\\\"content\\\"]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(l for l in u.splitlines() if l.startswith((\\\"Thesis\\\", \\\"Ladder\\\", \\\"[Not shown\\\", \\\"[Previous\\\")) or re.match(r\\\"\"'^- v'\"\\\\d+.*(?:H200|authoriz)\\\",l,re.I))); print(case);\nfor arm in (\\\"v7\\\",\\\"v7-noprev\\\"):\n for k in (1,2,3):\n  x=json.loads((root/\\\"goldprobe\\\"/arm/(\\\"{}-{}.json\\\".format(a,k))).read_text()); z=x[\\\"answer\\\"]; print(arm,k,z[\\\"rung\\\"],x[\\\"agrees\\\"],z[\\\"reasons\\\"],z[\\\"theme_pushes\\\"]);'\"","aggregated_output":"Thesis v17 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA's share of China's data-center AI accelerator spending in calendar 2026\", 2026, due 2027-03-31): What share of China's calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: NVIDIA's share of China's data-center AI accelerator spending is at least 30%. / rung 2 Bullish: NVIDIA's share of China's data-center AI accelerator spending is at least 15% and below 30%. / rung 3 Neutral: NVIDIA's share of China's data-center AI accelerator spending is at least 5% and below 15%. / rung 4 Bearish: NVIDIA's share of China's data-center AI accelerator spending is at least 1% and below 5%. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: NVIDIA's share of China's data-center AI accelerator spending is below 1%.\n- v25 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-14; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: There is no separate consensus supplied. The reported Chinese plan to let selected companies buy H200s is the directional reference and sits at rung 1 (Yes). But the newer, direct report that Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy H200s points the forecast toward no authorization by the d\n- v8 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-07-14; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (No): no Chinese authorization is established in the evidence, and the reported status quo is that China had kept Nvidia out despite U.S. export clearance. But the forecast is for the outcome by January 31, 2027, not whether authorization has already been confirmed. Reports t\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 4; reasons: There is no explicit consensus for NVIDIA's CY2026 share. The available reference is the current China run-rate: Q1 had no H20 shipments and Q2 guidance excludes China Data Center compute revenue, which sits at rung 5, but that is not a full-year forecast. I expect a low-single-digit share, around 2%, as a limited late-year opening is more likely than no sales, while domestic substitution and Huawei's position make a share of 5% or more unlikely. This crosses into rung 4 (1% to below 5%) but not rung 3. The global FY2027 Data Center revenue conclusion is consistent with this small China share and does not imply a higher one.\n{'case': 'G-d3-q17', 'draw': 'd3', 'qid': 'q17', 'view_id': 'v17', 'request_sha256': '5c3a03ecce04390976389bba7ee79d335537ecc2118062b3a6415c868f6e7b32', 'stored_rung': 4, 'stored_agrees': True, 'rungs': [{'position': 1, 'label': 'Strongly bullish', 'lo': 30.0, 'hi': None}, {'position': 2, 'label': 'Bullish', 'lo': 15.0, 'hi': 30.0}, {'position': 3, 'label': 'Neutral', 'lo': 5.0, 'hi': 15.0}, {'position': 4, 'label': 'Bearish', 'lo': 1.0, 'hi': 5.0}, {'position': 5, 'label': 'Strongly bearish', 'lo': None, 'hi': 1.0}]}\nv7 1 4 True No explicit market consensus for NVIDIA's CY2026 China share is supplied. The best reference is the current run-rate—zero H20 shipments in Q1 FY2027 and no China Data Center compute revenue in Q2 guidance—which sits at rung 5, below 1%. The forecast is higher than that reference because U.S. approval for two named Chinese buyers to purchase H200s makes some late-year sales possible, though the reported licensed shipments remain very small and no quantity for China is given. Domestic substitution and continued restrictions keep the likely share low; the implied low-single-digit outcome remains above the 1% rung-4 floor but well below rung 3's 5% boundary. The global Data Center revenue dependency does not establish a China-specific sales mix. [{'view_id': 'v8', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}]\nv7 2 4 True There is no explicit consensus for NVIDIA's CY2026 China share. The closest reference is the current operating run-rate: zero H20 shipments and Q2 FY2027 guidance excluding China Data Center compute revenue, which maps to rung 5 (<1%) but is not a full-year forecast. The forecast is modestly above that reference because U.S. approval for two buyers to purchase H200s creates a route to some late-year sales; however, the Chinese market remains restricted and a U.S. official described licensed shipments as “a very small quantity.” Domestic-budget and capacity evidence makes a material NVIDIA share unlikely. The implied low-single-digit share remains below 5%, so the forecast is rung 4. [{'view_id': 'v8', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}]\nv7 3 4 True There is no quantified consensus for NVIDIA's calendar-2026 China share. The observable market reference is the current zero-sales run-rate, rung 5, alongside Bloomberg Intelligence's qualitative expectation that NVIDIA's share will shrink. The forecast is slightly above that reference: the mid-July U.S. approvals create a route to limited second-half H200 sales, but China had barred NVIDIA, Q1 shipments were zero, Q2 guidance excluded China compute revenue, and licensed shipments were still described as very small. That supports a low-single-digit share, near the 1% boundary, rather than a return to the historical sales level; domestic substitution keeps it below 5%. The FY2027 global Data Center revenue conclusion does not imply a larger China share. [{'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v8', 'push': 'toward_first'}]\nv7-noprev 1 5 False The reference is effectively a near-zero NVIDIA share, rung 5: the evidence describes China as keeping NVIDIA out, with no H20 shipments and China excluded from current-quarter Data Center guidance. The forecast remains below 1%, rather than treating that current state as proof of the full-year outcome: U.S. approvals for two buyers create some upside, but licensed shipments were still described as very few, while Chinese sourcing and Huawei supply are expanding. The evidence therefore does not imply enough 2026 sales to cross the 1% boundary. This is consistent with v2's global Data Center revenue conclusion; it supplies no China-specific sales figure that would change this estimate. [{'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v8', 'push': 'toward_first'}]\nv7-noprev 2 5 False No explicit consensus for NVIDIA’s CY2026 China spending share is supplied. The nearest reference is NVIDIA’s Q2 FY2027 guidance excluding China Data Center compute revenue, which implies a near-zero share and sits at rung 5; that reference is only an anchor, not the reason to stay. The evidence still points to a near-zero CY2026 outcome: there were no H20 shipments in Q1, Q2 guidance excludes China, and the newly approved H200 route has produced only “very few” shipments. Domestic substitution and Huawei’s position add downside pressure. Limited H200 sales could make the share nonzero, but the evidence does not imply enough volume to reach the 1% boundary. This is consistent with the supplied global Data Center revenue conclusion for NVIDIA (v2). [{'view_id': 'v8', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}]\nv7-noprev 3 5 False There is no supplied consensus estimate for NVIDIA’s calendar-2026 China spending share. The status-quo reference is effectively zero China compute revenue, placing the reference at rung 5. The forecast also remains below 1%: zero H20 shipments and guidance excluding China revenue establish a near-zero starting run-rate, while the subsequent H200 approvals have produced only “a very small quantity of chips.” Domestic suppliers’ reported budget share and the domestic-supply policy reinforce the pressure on NVIDIA, though neither directly measures its share of calendar-2026 accelerator spending. Those data, and Huawei’s reported share of the broader AI-chip market, should not be treated as exact measures for this question. The H200 approvals create some upside risk, but the evidence does not imply enough shipments to cross the 1% boundary. The global Data Center revenue conclusion in v2 is consistent with this forecast but does not determine China’s share. The policy themes conflict: v8’s Yes conclusion pushes upward, while v25’s No conclusion pushes downward. [{'view_id': 'v8', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v25', 'push': 'toward_last'}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '326,356p'; ls -1 poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/deck-full/round-2 | head -15; for cid in C035 C068 C082 C073 C095 C102 C100 C108 C119 C043 C116 C123; do printf '\\\\n%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$cid\"; rg -n '\"'\"'^(Question:|[1-5]'\"\\\\. (NVIDIA|The|At|Below|Less|More)|Latest answer|Reason given|.*\\\\\"'$18 billion.*(25|obligation|rest)|.*'\"\\\\\"'$25 billion.*(inve|obligation))'\"' \\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/deck-full/\"'$cid.txt\" | cut -c1-540 | head -13; done'","aggregated_output":"   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\nC002-claude.json\nC002-codex.json\nC004-claude.json\nC004-codex.json\nC016-claude.json\nC016-codex.json\nC017-claude.json\nC017-codex.json\nC018-claude.json\nC018-codex.json\nC023-claude.json\nC023-codex.json\nC058-claude.json\nC058-codex.json\nC075-claude.json\n\nC035\n1:Question: How much will NVIDIA’s committed equity-investment obligations to ecosystem partners total at the FY2027 annual report?\n5:1. The disclosed amount is below $35 billion.\n6:2. The disclosed amount is at least $35 billion and below $60 billion.\n7:3. The disclosed amount is at least $60 billion and below $80 billion.\n8:4. The disclosed amount is at least $80 billion and below $100 billion.\n9:5. The disclosed amount is at least $100 billion.\n11:Latest answer at the cutoff: The disclosed amount is at least $35 billion and below $60 billion.\n12:Reason given: Reference: No market consensus is supplied. The closest issuer-disclosed reference is $25 billion of equity-investment commitments outstanding as of July 26, 2026, which sits in rung 1 (below $35 billion). Implied outcome: About $40 billion outstanding at the FY2027 annual report, placing the forecast in rung 2. The $25 billion July 26 balance plus $18 billion committed for the remainder of FY2027 gives roughly $43 billion gross; allowing for some of those commitments to be funded by year-end, while recognizing subseq\n100:43. (party_statement; publisher NVIDIA Corporation; speaker NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; published 2026-08-26) NVIDIA reported $99 billion of equity investments and $25 billion of equity investment commitments as of July 26, 2026.\n126:56. (party_statement; publisher businessinsider.com; speaker Business Insider; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; published 2026-08-26) NVIDIA said it had $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of FY2027, in addition to $47.9 billion already held in private companies.\n127:   Quote: The company said Wednesday that it has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year, on top of $47.9 billion it already holds in private companies.\n129:   Quote: Nvidia has also earmarked $18 billion for equity investments through the rest of this fiscal year\n132:59. (fact; publisher gurufocus.com; speaker gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA; published 2026-08-28) NVIDIA reported $99 billion in equity investments and $25 billion in equity-investment commitments.\n\nC068\n1:Question: How much will NVIDIA’s committed equity-investment obligations to ecosystem partners total at the FY2027 annual report?\n5:1. The disclosed amount is below $35 billion.\n6:2. The disclosed amount is at least $35 billion and below $60 billion.\n7:3. The disclosed amount is at least $60 billion and below $80 billion.\n8:4. The disclosed amount is at least $80 billion and below $100 billion.\n9:5. The disclosed amount is at least $100 billion.\n11:Latest answer at the cutoff: The disclosed amount is at least $35 billion and below $60 billion.\n12:Reason given: Reference: No market consensus is supplied. NVIDIA's reported $25 billion of equity-investment commitments outstanding as of July 26 is the closest company-reported reference and sits in rung 1 (below $35 billion). Implied outcome: About $40 billion at the FY2027 annual report. The $25 billion reported balance plus the $18 billion committed for the rest of FY2027 gives a $43 billion gross guide; allowing for possible overlap and commitments funded before year-end, while accounting for newly announced sized investments\n100:43. (party_statement; publisher NVIDIA Corporation; speaker NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; published 2026-08-26) N